{"route":"/docs/4.4/utilities/position/","version":"4.4","renderedVersion":"4.4","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Position","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use these shorthand utilities for quickly configuring the position of an element."},"blocks":[{"id":"common-values","type":"heading","en":"Common values","level":2},{"id":"common-values--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Quick positioning classes are available, though they are not responsive."},{"id":"common-values--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"position-static\">...</div>\n<div class=\"position-relative\">...</div>\n<div class=\"position-absolute\">...</div>\n<div class=\"position-fixed\">...</div>\n<div class=\"position-sticky\">...</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"fixed-top","type":"heading","en":"Fixed top","level":2},{"id":"fixed-top--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Position an element at the top of the viewport, from edge to edge. Be sure you understand the ramifications of fixed position in your project; you may need to add additional CSS."},{"id":"fixed-top--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"fixed-top\">...</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"fixed-bottom","type":"heading","en":"Fixed bottom","level":2},{"id":"fixed-bottom--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Position an element at the bottom of the viewport, from edge to edge. Be sure you understand the ramifications of fixed position in your project; you may need to add additional CSS."},{"id":"fixed-bottom--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"fixed-bottom\">...</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"sticky-top","type":"heading","en":"Sticky top","level":2},{"id":"sticky-top--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Position an element at the top of the viewport, from edge to edge, but only after you scroll past it. The <code>.sticky-top</code> utility uses CSS’s <code>position: sticky</code>, which isn’t fully supported in all browsers."},{"id":"sticky-top--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"<strong>IE11 and IE10 will render <code>position: sticky</code> as <code>position: relative</code>.</strong> As such, we wrap the styles in a <code>@supports</code> query, limiting the stickiness to only browsers that can render it properly."},{"id":"sticky-top--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"sticky-top\">...</div>","language":"html"}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Getting started","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Theming","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/theming/"},{"en":"Build tools","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/build-tools/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/accessibility/"},{"en":"Layout","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/overview/"},{"en":"Overview","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/overview/"},{"en":"Grid","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/grid/"},{"en":"Utilities for layout","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/utilities-for-layout/"},{"en":"Content","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/content/reboot/"},{"en":"Reboot","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/content/reboot/"},{"en":"Typography","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/content/typography/"},{"en":"Code","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/content/code/"},{"en":"Images","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/d